# Space Cake -- vanilla's cake with the strawberries swapped for hemp.
#
# Every MATRIX below is the matching vanilla cake texture extracted verbatim; only the PALETTE
# is ours, and it moves in exactly two ways:
#
#   * the four strawberry reds map, in luminance order, onto a hemp-leaf green ramp. That is the
#     whole visual idea -- a cake iced with herb instead of fruit reads instantly and needs no new
#     shape. Greens run slightly darker than the reds they replace, which is correct: herb is not
#     as bright as a strawberry.
#   * the sponge browns take a mild olive shift (R x0.92, G x1.10, B x0.90), and exactly ONE
#     tone per texture is pushed the rest of the way to hemp green so there are flecks through
#     the batter as well as icing on top. The sponge stays sponge-coloured: a cake whose crumb
#     is solid green is a cliche, and it also stops reading as cake. Creams and whites are
#     untouched, because a space cake is still a cake.
#
# PLACEHOLDER: derived art, not drawn. Redraw or retone freely -- to retone, change the greens
# or the olive factors and re-render.

@palette space_cake_top
. = none
1 = 2F4D1D
2 = 3E5F24
3 = 486F2A
4 = 6F9438
5 = F6E8CB
6 = FDF4D8
7 = FFFDFE

